# libledger89

A durable, ordered, rewindable sequence of opaque byte records addressed by
stable logical positions, in strict ISO C89.

```text
                     index space
              first             end
                |                |
                v                v
          [ R ][ R ][ R ][ R ][   ]
            \____________/
              stable prefix

append       extends the right edge
sync         advances the stable edge
truncate     moves the right edge left (revision++)
prune        moves the left edge right
read         addresses one retained position
iterate      walks retained positions
```

libledger89 owns exactly one thing: a locally durable, ordered, rewindable
sequence of opaque byte records. It knows nothing about Raft terms, leaders,
message queues, SQL, indexes, queries, or application semantics, and it never
interprets record payloads.

## Boundaries

| Concern | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| record framing and checksums | `libledger89` |
| locally durable sequence numbering | `libledger89` |
| append batch atomicity | `libledger89` |
| explicit stable frontier (`stable_end`) | `libledger89` |
| part creation/sealing/rotation | `libledger89` |
| crash recovery and topology publication | `libledger89` |
| suffix truncation (`truncate_from`) | `libledger89`, explicit request |
| prefix pruning mechanism (`prune_before`) | `libledger89`, explicit request |
| retention policy | caller |
| replication, consensus | `libraft89` and an adapter |
| semantic record envelopes (WAL/MQ/Raft/IPC) | higher layers |
| secondary indexes, SQL, queries, projections | external query engine |

## Build and test

- `just build` — build `build/libledger89.a`.
- `just smoke` — one end-to-end open/append/sync/reopen/read path.
- `just unit` — codecs, checksums, scalar math, model filesystem.
- `just api` — black-box public API behavior.
- `just adapters` — WAL-style, replicated-log-style, and checkpoint consumers.
- `just crash` — crash sweeps over the model filesystem plus real process kills.
- `just fault`, `just fault-nomem`, `just fault-eintr` — I/O, allocation, EINTR.
- `just corrupt` — structural corruption classification.
- `just model` — randomized reference-model comparison.
- `just golden` — frozen byte fixtures; regenerate with `just golden-gen`.
- `just stress` — many parts, huge payload, large batches.
- `just test` — all fast suites, including the strict fast tier.
- `just long` — multi-hundred-thousand-operation model run plus a many-part sweep.
- `just sanitize` — fast suites under ASan + UBSan.
- `just valgrind` — fast suites under valgrind memcheck.
- `just strict-fast` — ctypes + runner strict subset (<2 min).
- `just strict` — full strict tier: fault, crash, corruption, model, adversarial.
- `just strict-long` — long tier: exhaustive corruption, 2M-op model, large sweeps.
- `just strict-sanitize` / `just strict-valgrind` — runner-based strict subsets
  under ASan+UBSan and memcheck.
- `just gen-strict-tables` — regenerate the committed strict-suite case tables.
- `just ratio` — enforce the 10:1 test:source NLOC gate.
- `just coverage` / `just coverage-report` — enforce 95% line / 90% branch
  coverage of `src/` and print the HTML report.
- `just green` — green conformance matrix (see the status note below).
- `just check` — green profile, lint, all fast suites, ratio, and coverage.

## Green conformance

`just green` reports CGREEN PASS: GCC and Clang in both C89 and C23 modes,
the clang-tidy semantic checks, and the canonical format all pass. `just
check` runs the green matrix, lint, and the full fast test suite.

## Conventions

- Public API namespaced `ledger89_*`, declared in `include/ledger89.h`.
- On-disk format v2 is little-endian with CRC-32C; no native structs.
- `CURRENT` selects the committed manifest; stable markers select the durable
  frontier inside the active part.
- Test-driven: scenario -> acceptance -> failing test -> minimal code ->
  refactor.
- `main` stays green; no commits or pushes without permission.

See `spec/ledger89-spec.md` for the normative contract and `.agent/` for the
concept, design, scenarios, and acceptance criteria.
